    },
    {
      "id": "97046645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the major : Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Helpful resources: Academic Catalog Transfer Admissions Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the Stanislaus State Articulation Website for contact information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>This agreement displays all<strong> lower-division courses required in the major</strong>: Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful resources: </strong></p><p><a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Catalog</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/undergrad/transfer-admission\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admissions</a></p><p><br></p><p>Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the <a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/articulation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Stanislaus State Articulation Website</a> for contact information.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "5dc07645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "85ce7645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "History provides a general background for studying the humanities or social sciences and understanding the contemporary world. Preparation in history is especially useful for careers which require careful judgment on the basis of evidence, such as law and journalism, as well as teaching and a variety of local, state, or federal government positions, including the United States Foreign Service. A History degree also provides excellent preparation for careers in museum and archival work, and is desirable for any profession that requires well developed skills in critical thinking and writing. The Department of History supports the concept of international education and encourages students to investigate opportunities for overseas study described in the International Education section of the catalog. View information for the Department of History , including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>History provides a general background for studying the humanities or social sciences and understanding the contemporary world. Preparation in history is especially useful for careers which require careful judgment on the basis of evidence, such as law and journalism, as well as teaching and a variety of local, state, or federal government positions, including the United States Foreign Service. A History degree also provides excellent preparation for careers in museum and archival work, and is desirable for any profession that requires well developed skills in critical thinking and writing.</p><p><br></p><p>The Department of History supports the concept of international education and encourages students to investigate opportunities for overseas study described in the International Education section of the catalog.</p><p><br></p><p>View information for the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=35&amp;ent_oid=1723\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Department of History</a>, including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f03f7445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Reading knowledge of a foreign language is desirable but not required for the bachelor’s degree and the history graduate program.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Reading knowledge of a foreign language is desirable but not required for the bachelor’s degree and the history graduate program.</p>"
    }
  ],
